mn36:3.3 starts: and said to the Blessed One:
mn36:19.12 starts: These are the three similes that occurred
mn36:21.3 starts: So I stopped the in-breaths and out-breaths
mn36:35-37.3 starts: With the fading away as well of rapture
mn36:35-37.5 starts: With the abandoning of pleasure and pain
mn36:35-37.6 starts: But such pleasant feeling that arose in me
mn36:40.2 starts: …as MN4, §29… Thus with the divine eye
mn36:42.2 starts: I directly knew as it actually is:
mn36:43.3 starts: I directly knew:
